{"name":"Pink Flambé","hex":"#cd4e82","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pink","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A color reminiscent of pinks, the flowers.","Magenta, the colour evoked by red and blue light when combined."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a colour between red and white; pale red.","Of a fox-hunter's jacket: scarlet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pink"},{"term":"flambé","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Being, or having been, flambéed.","Decorated by glaze splashed or irregularly spread upon the surface, or apparently applied at the top and allowed to run down the sides."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A showy cooking technique where an alcoholic beverage, such as brandy, is added to hot food and then the fumes are ignited.","A flambéed dish."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flamb%C3%A9"}],"entries":[{"title":"Flambé","blocks":[{"text":"Flambé is a cooking procedure in which alcohol is added to a hot pan to create a burst of flames. The word means \"flamed\" in French."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Banana_flamb%C3%A9_-_by_Jenene.jpg/330px-Banana_flamb%C3%A9_-_by_Jenene.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flamb%C3%A9","wikidata":"Q386003"},{"title":"Pink","blocks":[{"text":"Pink is a pale tint of red or rose, the color of the pink flower. It was first used as a color name in the late 17th century. A combination of pink and white is associated with innocence, whereas a combination of pink and black links to eroticism and seduction."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg/330px-Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pink","wikidata":"Q429220"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedi